**Critical insight:** The annihilator `g(x) = 1 + x_0 + x_1 + x_{0,1} = (1 + x_0)(1 + x_1)` is the SAME polynomial for ALL N from 5 to 13. This polynomial equals 1 iff `n ≡ 0 mod 4` — and no prime > 2 is divisible by 4 (and chi_P(2) is also annihilated since bit_1(2)=1). 

So AI(chi_P) = 2 is exactly the mod-4 sieve structure. This is the polynomial-method analogue of the Hardy-Littlewood / W-trick effect. The wild swing is now: **does AI(chi_P) > 2 after the W-trick?**
