    679	
    680	Define the normalized Gowers uniformity norm `Q^k(f) := ||f||_{U^k}^{2^k} / E[f]^{2^k}`
    681	on `Z/NZ`. Hardy-Littlewood for the {0,1}^k-cube prime k-tuple
    682	configuration predicts
    683	
    684	   `Q^k(chi_P) -> S_k    as N -> infinity,`
    685	   `S_k = product_p alpha_p(k) / (1 - 1/p)^{2^k},`
    686	   `alpha_p(k) = #{(x, h_1, ..., h_k) in (Z/p)^{k+1} : x + epsilon . h != 0 for all epsilon in {0,1}^k} / p^{k+1}`.
    687	
    688	Numerically (direct enumeration in `(Z/p)^{k+1}`, product truncated):
    689	
    690	  `S_2 = 2.300938`   (truncation error <= 1e-5 at P_max = 100)
    691	  `S_3 = 54.116088`  (truncation error ~ 0.2% at P_max = 47)
    692	
    693	Empirically (cyclic Z/N, FFT for U^2, recursion for U^3):
    694	
    695	  `Q^2(chi_P)`: 2.103 (N=2^10) → 2.132 (N=2^12) → 2.146 (N=2^14)
    696	                → 2.149 (N=2^16) → 2.153 (N=2^18). Trends monotonically to S_2.
    697	  `Q^3(chi_P)`: 35.5 +- 0.1 across N ∈ [2^10, 2^13]; far above the
    698	                random-Bernoulli baseline (which → 1) but slow to
    699	                approach S_3 = 54 due to compounded finite-N corrections.
