c ≥ 0.78 → mean min_M = 5.50; [0.75, 0.78) → 5.67; [0.72, 0.75) → 6.40 (the M=7 region); < 0.72 → 5.00 (low-weight compensation). The (bit_0_acc, weight, min_M) surface is the structural explanation. **Closure mode C** (circular): the depth-2 gap is fully captured by an elementary fact already in the project's frame (bit_0 "free first gate" mechanism, S84 §"Mechanism: single-bit predictor advantage"); calibration formally verifies the explanation. Recommends footnote on `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`: 36th measure (depth-2 sign-threshold) DEVIATES from unbiased random but the deviation is fully captured by the trivial 1-bit oddness fact; pseudorandomness thesis stands "modulo the obvious mod-2 bias." **Net new content**: (a) verified S84 mechanism (bit_0 → depth-2 size) under direct calibrated control; (b) new mechanism prediction empirically confirmed (bit_0_acc-vs-min_M monotonic at fixed weight); (c) PRIMES-vs-calibrated indistinguishability removes the only known deviation in the 35+ measure battery from "structural" to "elementary parity" status. Spawned successor C7.a (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — N=8 calibrated extension. Cites E1.10, E3.13, E1.6, E1.4, S84. See experiments/circuit_complexity/sat_tc0_primes_n8_calibrated/. | 89 |
