## Session 95 — Frontier attack on §D7 — DPP / PPP fit complete.

**Target:** ATTACK_VECTORS §D.D7 (Determinantal Point Process fit to integer prime sequence).
**Channel:** Tao. **Cross-domain technique:** Determinantal Point Processes (first project use; was PROPOSED-only).
**Self-grade: B-grade** (clean structural negative; ambitious frontier attack with all 5 pre-stated falsifiers HOLD).

### Result in one paragraph

Primes are quantitatively NOT a translation-invariant DPP, PPP, signed-real-K, or complex-Hermitian-K point process. At pair level, `R_2 - ρ²` flips sign across odd/even (DPP needs ≤0, PPP needs ≥0), ruling out either. Restricted to the all-even sub-lattice, PPP overshoots HL by 7.5–79.2% across 19 admissible 3-tuples (max on 3-AP triples (0,6,12), (0,12,18), (0,18,24)). Real-signed K with magnitudes from pair correlations gives required cross-term σ_req ∈ (-0.541, +0.769), never ±1. Complex-Hermitian K best phase residual 0.0746 ≫ 0.01 noise floor. **Mechanism:** HL singular series factorises over PRIMES; DPP/PPP factorises over PAIRS; pair admissibility ≠ triple admissibility (e.g., (0, 4, 14) is pair-admissible mod 3 but ν₃=3 saturates).

### New edge **E2.16**

First 3-point structural statement ruling out kernel factorisation, complementing the 2-point closures E2.13 (Gowers, S85), E2.14 (Anderson, S88), E2.15 (algebraic immunity, S92) — fourth orthogonal mathematical category and first 3-point level.

