    ## Main Result
    
    The Bourgain-Glibichuk-Konyagin theorem provides a 'sum-product' theorem for subsets A of the finite field F_p (p prime), giving a lower bound on max(|A+A|, |A·A|).
    
    ## Statement and Exponent
    
    An explicit version of this estimate shows that if 1 < |A| ≤ p^(7/13)(log p)^(-4/13), then max{|A+A|, |A·A|} >> |A|^(15/14) / (log|A|)^(2/7).
    
    ## Applications
    
    The Bourgain-Glibichuk-Konyagin bounds are particularly useful for obtaining exponential sum estimates over subgroups, and as a byproduct they provide a clean proof of the Bourgain-Katz-Tao theorem on the sum-product phenomenon in F_p.
    
    ## Main Technical Result
    
    The second and main result of the theorem provides new bounds on exponential sums of the form ∑_{x_1,...,x_k∈A} exp(2πi x_1⋯x_k ξ/p).
    
    
