    759:| §C4 ATTACK_VECTORS — Anderson localisation Lyapunov exponent gamma(E) of chi_P-driven discrete 1D Schrödinger operator (cross-domain: Aizenman-Warzel random operators, Furstenberg-Kifer theorem) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether chi_P deviates from random pseudorandomness on a SPECTRAL-GLOBAL statistic (Lyapunov exponent) — orthogonal to all 36 prior pseudorandomness measures (which are local correlation / entropy / Fourier / tensor rank / Gowers). Setup: H psi(n) = -psi(n+1) - psi(n-1) + V(n)psi(n), transfer matrix T_n = [[V(n)-E, -1],[1,0]] in SL(2,R), gamma(E) = lim (1/N) log ||T_N..T_1||. Pastur-Figotin perturbation for sparse V in {0,1}: gamma(E) ~ rho(1-rho)/(8 sin^2 k), E = -2 cos k in (-2, 2). Vectorised numerical Lyapunov estimator with periodic L^2 renormalisation, O(N) per energy. **Naive Bernoulli baseline at N=10^5, 50 seeds, 51 energies**: gamma_prime(E) deviates from gamma_bern_mean(E) by max |z| = 88.5 sigma at E = 0.108 (k = pi/2 parity resonance). Z-score grows as sqrt(N): 12.3 at N=10^4 → 88.5 at N=10^5. **Confounder: chi_P concentrated on odd indices.** Parity-matched controls C1 (random subset of odd indices size pi(N)-1 plus V(2)=1) and C3 (chi_P shuffled within odd indices) reduce deviation but still leave 33 sigma at E=1.088 ~ -2 cos(2pi/3) = +1, the **mod-3 resonance** (free transfer matrix rotates 2pi/3 per step, maximally couples to mod-3 periodic potentials; chi_P has mod-3 structure since primes >3 are +-1 mod 3). **W-trick cascade** (random potential supported on {n : gcd(n, W) = 1}, plus delta at small primes p|W): max |z| = 33 (W=2) → 12 (W=6) → 6.3 (W=30) → 6.1 (W=210) → 4.0 (W=2310, N=2*10^5). Cascade ends at residual ~ 4 sigma, borderline noise (Bonferroni 0.05/31 → z_thresh ≈ 3.16). **Same structural reason as E2.13/S85** (Gowers U^k of chi_P → Hardy-Littlewood singular series, recovered by W-trick): chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure. Adds new EDGE E2.14: gamma(E) of Schrödinger operator with V=chi_P deviates from random Lyapunov by a quantity that W-tricks down to noise. **Closure mode E**: deviation IS the spectral signature of Hardy-Littlewood / Bombieri-Vinogradov equidistribution mod q; no additional spectral structure beyond what equidistribution already gives; algorithmic gamma extraction costs Theta(N), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: transfer-matrix product / Lyapunov machinery (Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators*, Furstenberg-Kifer 1983) had never been applied to chi_P; the spectral signature of the W-trick at the Anderson-Lyapunov level is novel. **PROVIDES SECOND INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION** (after E2.13/S85) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, in a category orthogonal to additive combinatorics. Cites E2.13, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 (AMS GSM 168); Furstenberg-Kifer 1983 Israel J. Math. 46; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/dynamical/anderson_localisation_chi_p/anderson_localisation_chi_p_results.md. | 88 |
    760:| §B1 ATTACK_VECTORS — slice rank / Croot-Lev-Pach polynomial method on chi_P, via algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (cross-domain: cap-set polynomial method, Tao slice rank, Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether the cap-set polynomial-method machinery yields a polylog primality witness via low-degree annihilators of chi_P. Three structurally distinct invariants: (1) algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (smallest deg g with g·chi_P==0 or g·(1+chi_P)==0); (2) F_p multilinear ANF degree on (F_p)^k via base-p expansion; (3) slice rank brackets via Tao 2016 flattening lower bound + greedy upper bound. **Main empirical finding**: AI(chi_P, N) = 2 for ALL N in [4, 13] while AI(matched-density Bernoulli) grows as Theta(log_2(1/rho)) — reaching 4 at N=11/12 with zero std. Liouville+ AI grows like random; Mobius!=0 also has constant AI=2. **Mechanism (extracted via nullspace recovery)**: the unique smallest annihilator is the SAME polynomial g(x) = (1 + x_0)(1 + x_1) for every N >= 5, which equals 1 iff n ≡ 0 mod 4. The annihilation works because no prime > 2 is divisible by 4 (and chi_P(2) gets killed by bit_1=1). AI(chi_P)=2 is *exactly* the polynomial-method encoding of the trivial mod-4 sieve fact; same g annihilates Mobius!=0 because squarefree numbers exclude multiples of 4. Liouville+ does NOT inherit this since lambda(4)=+1. **W-trick correction CONFIRMS deviation is mod-q structure**: at W=6, b∈{1,5} and W=30, b∈{1,7,11}, AI(chi_P_{W,b}) tracks AI(random) within ±1 across N=8..11; many cells exact match with zero std (e.g. W=6 b=1 N=11: chi_P=5, random=5.00 std 0). **F_p multilinear ANF degree**: chi_P near-saturates max possible degree (p-1)·k at all tested (p,k) other than (3,3) where deg drops 1 below random max, and (5,3) similar single-degree drop. **Slice rank brackets**: at p=2 non-informative (2-row flattenings cap rank at 2 trivially, both chi_P and random); at p=3 chi_P matches random for k>=3. **Same structural reason as E2.13 (Gowers, S85), E2.14 (Anderson, S88)**: chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure; the polynomial-method invariant gives no additional bit beyond mod-q. **Adds EDGE E2.15**: AI_F_2(chi_P) = 2 for all N >= 4 with explicit annihilator (1+x_0)(1+x_1); W-trick at W>=6 removes deviation. THIRD INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers and E2.14/S88 Anderson) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a third orthogonal mathematical category (Boolean polynomial method / algebraic cryptanalysis). **Closure mode E**: AI deviation IS the polynomial-method encoding of the mod-4 sieve fact; no additional polynomial-method content beyond mod-q. AI extraction itself is exponential time in N (LP over 2^N x sum_i C(N,i) F_2 monomial-evaluation matrix), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: Croot-Lev-Pach / Tao slice rank / Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity machinery had never been applied to chi_P; the polynomial-method signature of the W-trick at AI level is novel. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Croot-Lev-Pach arXiv:1605.01506; Tao 2016 blog (slice rank); Ellenberg-Gijswijt 2017 Annals 185, 339; Courtois-Meier 2003 Eurocrypt LNCS 2656; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/algebraic/algebraic_immunity_chi_p/algebraic_immunity_chi_p_results.md. | 92 |
    761:| §D7 ATTACK_VECTORS — Determinantal point process (DPP) / permanantal counterpart fit to integer prime sequence (cross-domain: DPP theory, Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009, Soshnikov 2000, Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether chi_P admits a translation-invariant kernel representation R_2(t) = rho^2 ± K(t)^2 (DPP -, PPP +). Tested four progressively-flexible kernel hypotheses at N = 10^7. **F1 (DPP pair-level)**: K^2_DPP(t) = rho^2 - R_2(t) < 0 at ALL 15 admissible even t in [2, 30]; HL gives S(0, t) > 1 ⇒ R_2 > rho^2. Pair-level DPP infeasible. **F2 (PPP pair-level)**: K^2_PPP(t) = R_2(t) - rho^2 < 0 at ALL 14 odd t > 1 (R_2 ≈ 0). Pair-level PPP infeasible. Sign of (R_2 - rho^2) flips between odd/even — no real translation-invariant K. **F3 (PPP 3-point)** restricting to all-even sub-lattice where K^2_PPP > 0: permanent prediction R_3^PPP overshoots HL prediction R_3^HL = rho^3 S(0, t_1, t_2) by 7.5–79.2% across 19 admissible triples (max gap on 3-AP triples (0,6,12), (0,12,18), (0,18,24)). **F4 (real-signed K)**: with magnitudes |K(t)| = rho sqrt(S(0,t)-1) and signs s : t → ±1, required cross-term σ_req ∈ (-0.541, +0.769), NEVER ±1 (closest 0.769) at any of 19 admissible triples. Real signed K of right magnitudes fails universally. **F5 (complex Hermitian K)**: phases free; least-squares fit of φ over 13 distinct offsets (200 random starts, LM + trust-region) yields best max residual 0.0746 ≫ 0.01 noise floor. No globally consistent phase assignment. **Inadmissibility blindness**: PPP predicts non-zero R_3 for inadmissible triples like (0, 4, 14) (where ν_3 = 3 saturates) because pair correlations alone cannot detect multi-body admissibility. **Mechanism**: HL singular series factorises over PRIMES (∏_p α_p(0, t_1, ..., t_k) with α_p depending on ν_p = #distinct residues mod p); DPP/PPP correlations factorise over PAIRS. Pairwise admissibility ≠ triple admissibility. **Adds EDGE E2.16**: primes are NOT a translation-invariant DPP / PPP / signed-real-K / complex-Hermitian-K point process. FOURTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers, E2.14/S88 Anderson, E2.15/S92 algebraic immunity) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a FOURTH orthogonal mathematical category (point-process theory) AND at the 3-point level (prior three were 2-point). **Closure mode I**: HL prime-by-prime factorisation cannot reduce to pair-level kernel. Cross-domain ingredient (DPP) performed real work; first project use. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009 *Zeros of GAFs and DPPs* (AMS ULect 51); Soshnikov 2000 (arXiv:math/0002099); Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP. See experiments/constructions/primes_dpp_ppp_fit/primes_dpp_ppp_fit_results.md. | 95 |
