## Session 100 — G1 Liouville Anderson Lyapunov — **B-grade**

**Wild swing target.** ATTACK_VECTORS §G1 (highest-leverage frontier per the §G framing — "the project's current highest-leverage frontier" — multiplicative regime beyond W-trick wall). Pre-stated F1 (A-grade) was sustained `|z| > 5` not removable by W-trick.

**Result.** F1 false; F2 (B-grade) holds strongly. At three sample sizes (N=10⁵, 3×10⁵, 10⁶), `γ_λ(E)` matches Rademacher to within seed noise (max |z| flat at 1.78–2.16), the argmax energy wanders, χ²/K is sub-Rademacher (0.49–0.69), Pastur-Figotin agreement is identical to 4 decimals, and an independent Chowla two-point aggregate at N=10⁶ gives Σz² = 4.77 vs χ²₁₆=16. Stark contrast with chi_P (E2.14): 88σ at N=10⁵ requiring W=2310 to suppress; lambda needs no W-trick.

**Why B not A.** No deviation found; the intended polylog opening (λ-side explicit-formula partial sum) is closed, not opened.

**Why B not C.** First project use of cross-domain technique "Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality" (Green-Tao 2012, Sarnak 2010, Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla), now USED-E with edge E2.18. Paired contrast with E2.14 isolates chi_P's spectral signal as exclusively HL mod-q resonance — a structural statement the project did not previously have.

**Files written.** New experiment dir `experiments/dynamical/liouville_anderson_lyapunov/` (5 files); EDGES.md adds E2.18; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgrades Anderson row + adds Möbius/nilsequence row; ATTACK_VECTORS.md §G1 → Closed attacks with G1.a/G1.b/G1.c successors; CLOSED_PATHS row; session 100 synthesis; SESSION_INSIGHTS appended; `.run_state` = 95.

**Next-action.** G1.c (heavy-tail Schrödinger V=log p_n on primes; introduces Bourgain-Goldstein-Schlag 2002 *Annals* 154 as new technique) or G2 (Gowers U^k of centered λ ∈ {-1,+1}, one-line script change from D6.b).
