    736	Refined statement: **S_k is the universal Gowers fingerprint of the
    737	{0,1}^k-cube prime correlation, independent of the weighting scheme
    738	applied to detect it (bare indicator chi_P or log-weighted Λ).**
    739	
    740	> Why this is an edge: **first project measure where chi_P
    741	> deviates from random by a CLOSED-FORM, predicted, constant
    742	> multiplicative factor (the Hardy-Littlewood singular series)**, in
    743	> contrast to the 35+ prior pseudorandomness measures that all
    744	> returned "indistinguishable from random". The deviation is exactly
    745	> the prime k-tuple correlation captured by HL — there is no
    746	> additional structure beyond HL. Combined with E2.9 (degree-d
    747	> Fourier weight BELOW random for d >= 2): chi_P's higher-order
    748	> structure is "exactly Hardy-Littlewood, no more". This narrows the
    749	> "what extra structure could chi_P have" search space.
    750	
    751	> Why this is **not** an algorithmic opening: extracting Q^k(chi_P)
    752	> empirically requires summing over (x, h) ∈ (Z/N)^{k+1}, cost
    753	> Theta(N^2 log N) at U^2 — already non-polylog. The structural
    754	> identity Q^k(chi_P) = S_k provides only the same information that
    755	> HL already gives, in compressed form.
