    1	# Session 101 — D6.c μ-weighted χ_P at U^2 — family-level refinement of E2.13
    2	
    3	**Mode:** novelty (B-grade target).
    4	**Target:** NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md §D6.c.
    5	**Self-grade:** **B**.
    6	
    7	## What was attempted
    8	
    9	The literal §D6.c question asks: does the function `μ(n)·χ_P(n)`
    10	"kill the Hardy-Littlewood structure" of χ_P at U^2 even before
    11	W-tricking? The proposed test was that `Q²(μ·χ_P) ≈ 1` (Gowers-
    12	uniform) would establish a bare-function equivalent of GT's Möbius
    13	orthogonality.
    14	
    15	## Key step: identify the literal collapse
    16	
    17	`μ(p) = −1` on every prime p (since ω(p) = 1, μ(squarefree, odd ω) = −1).
