    761:| §D7 ATTACK_VECTORS — Determinantal point process (DPP) / permanantal counterpart fit to integer prime sequence (cross-domain: DPP theory, Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009, Soshnikov 2000, Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether chi_P admits a translation-invariant kernel representation R_2(t) = rho^2 ± K(t)^2 (DPP -, PPP +). Tested four progressively-flexible kernel hypotheses at N = 10^7. **F1 (DPP pair-level)**: K^2_DPP(t) = rho^2 - R_2(t) < 0 at ALL 15 admissible even t in [2, 30]; HL gives S(0, t) > 1 ⇒ R_2 > rho^2. Pair-level DPP infeasible. **F2 (PPP pair-level)**: K^2_PPP(t) = R_2(t) - rho^2 < 0 at ALL 14 odd t > 1 (R_2 ≈ 0). Pair-level PPP infeasible. Sign of (R_2 - rho^2) flips between odd/even — no real translation-invariant K. **F3 (PPP 3-point)** restricting to all-even sub-lattice where K^2_PPP > 0: permanent prediction R_3^PPP overshoots HL prediction R_3^HL = rho^3 S(0, t_1, t_2) by 7.5–79.2% across 19 admissible triples (max gap on 3-AP triples (0,6,12), (0,12,18), (0,18,24)). **F4 (real-signed K)**: with magnitudes |K(t)| = rho sqrt(S(0,t)-1) and signs s : t → ±1, required cross-term σ_req ∈ (-0.541, +0.769), NEVER ±1 (closest 0.769) at any of 19 admissible triples. Real signed K of right magnitudes fails universally. **F5 (complex Hermitian K)**: phases free; least-squares fit of φ over 13 distinct offsets (200 random starts, LM + trust-region) yields best max residual 0.0746 ≫ 0.01 noise floor. No globally consistent phase assignment. **Inadmissibility blindness**: PPP predicts non-zero R_3 for inadmissible triples like (0, 4, 14) (where ν_3 = 3 saturates) because pair correlations alone cannot detect multi-body admissibility. **Mechanism**: HL singular series factorises over PRIMES (∏_p α_p(0, t_1, ..., t_k) with α_p depending on ν_p = #distinct residues mod p); DPP/PPP correlations factorise over PAIRS. Pairwise admissibility ≠ triple admissibility. **Adds EDGE E2.16**: primes are NOT a translation-invariant DPP / PPP / signed-real-K / complex-Hermitian-K point process. FOURTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers, E2.14/S88 Anderson, E2.15/S92 algebraic immunity) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a FOURTH orthogonal mathematical category (point-process theory) AND at the 3-point level (prior three were 2-point). **Closure mode I**: HL prime-by-prime factorisation cannot reduce to pair-level kernel. Cross-domain ingredient (DPP) performed real work; first project use. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009 *Zeros of GAFs and DPPs* (AMS ULect 51); Soshnikov 2000 (arXiv:math/0002099); Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP. See experiments/constructions/primes_dpp_ppp_fit/primes_dpp_ppp_fit_results.md. | 95 |
