    753:| C6 (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — three-pillars × HKM time-space tradeoff classification | REFINEMENT | I | Composition of E7.7 (three-pillars informational closure: prime positions / zeta zeros / floor values) and E6.7 (HKM at (T = N^{8/15}, S = N^{1/3})). Built (alpha, beta) catalog of 14 algorithms (4 prime / 4 zeta / 6 floor) and computed per-pillar Pareto frontiers, cross-pillar dominance, and saturation against E7.6 lower bound (T*S ≥ Ω(N^{5/6}/log N)). **Findings**: (i) HKM is on the floor-pillar Pareto frontier and DOMINATES every other floor-pillar entry elementwise (Lucy DP, Lucy+Fenwick, Meissel-Lehmer classical, Gourdon, primecount); (ii) HKM has NO cross-pillar dominators — its (8/15, 1/3) point is uniquely accessible on the floor pillar (no zero-pillar or prime-pillar entry achieves both T ≤ N^{8/15} AND S ≤ N^{1/3}); (iii) **pillar dominance regions are non-overlapping**: time-only minimum is shared by prime/zeta pillars at α=1/2, space-only minimum is unique to floor at β=1/3, T*S minimum is unique to floor at 13/15 ≈ 0.867; (iv) HKM saturates E7.6 to within N^{0.034} (gap 13/15 - 5/6 = 1/30); (v) Aggarwal binary search (E6.6) is a meta-algorithm whose effective placement migrates with the chosen pi(x) sub-routine. All four pre-stated falsification criteria (F1: HKM dominated; F2: HKM cross-pillar dominated; F3: identical pillar frontiers; F4: floor-pillar T*S < 5/6) PASS. **Net new content**: (a) explicit pillar-by-pillar Pareto map of the project's catalog; (b) HKM uniqueness lemma (HKM's (T, S) point is achievable on the floor pillar ONLY); (c) saturation verdict (floor pillar asymptotically tight). No polylog opening — refinement of E7.7 and E6.7, not a new edge. Cites E5.1, E6.5, E6.6, E6.7, E6.8, E6.9, E7.6, E7.7, E7.9. See experiments/constructions/pillar_tradeoff_diagram/. | 81 |
    758:| C7 (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — calibrated 1-bit-bias random control for the S84 PRIMES-vs-random depth-2 sign-threshold gap | REFINEMENT | C | Composition of E1.10 / E3.13 (35-measure pseudorandomness battery, `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`) + S84 result (PRIMES min M=6 vs unbiased matched-density random min M ∈ {7,8} at N=6, binomial p < 0.001). S84 conjectured the gap was driven by PRIMES's 1-bit-predictor advantage (bit_0 = "is x odd" gives 75.0% accuracy on PRIMES at N=6, vs ~66% for unbiased random of weight 18/64). C7 builds the matched-class-conditional random control `f_cal` on {0..63}: P(f_cal=1 \| x odd) = 17/32 (exactly matching PRIMES's 17 odd primes); P(f_cal=1 \| x even) = 1/32 (exactly matching PRIMES's 1 even prime, namely 2). Two modes: STRATIFIED (exact 17 odd + 1 even, weight always 18, bit_0_acc always 0.75) and BERNOULLI (independent draws; variable weight, variable bit_0_acc 0.625-0.81). 20 samples each through S84's `enum_d2_smart` ILP harness (K=1458 W=1 candidates, CBC, 120s/cell). **Pre-stated falsifiers (4 outcomes)**: F1 (≥1 stratified > 6 → residual structure), F2 (all stratified ≤ 6 → gap is oddness), F3 (≥1 stratified < 6 → calibration overshoots), F4 (stratified mean < unbiased mean → bit_0 primary driver). **Result: F2 + F3 + F4 HOLD; F1 FAILS.** Stratified histogram = {5: 4, 6: 16}, mean 5.80, max 6 — 0/20 above PRIMES; 4/20 *strictly easier* than PRIMES at M=5. Bernoulli histogram = {5: 7, 6: 11, 7: 2} — both M=7 cases have bit_0_acc < 0.75 (PRIMES's value: 0.7344 and 0.7188), empirically confirming the proposed monotonic relationship `bit_0_acc ↑ ⇒ min_M ↓` at fixed weight. PRIMES sits at +0.5σ of the calibrated distribution; under the calibrated null `P(M ≤ 6) = 1.0` (vs unbiased null `P(M ≤ 6) = 0/10 → 0.5^10 ≈ 0.001`). **The S84 PRIMES-vs-random gap REDUCES TO elementary parity** ("π(x) ≈ 1 iff x odd, for x > 2"); no PRIMES-specific structure beyond oddness. **Sub-finding** (Bernoulli stratified by bit_0_acc bins): bit_0_acc ≥ 0.78 → mean min_M = 5.50; [0.75, 0.78) → 5.67; [0.72, 0.75) → 6.40 (the M=7 region); < 0.72 → 5.00 (low-weight compensation). The (bit_0_acc, weight, min_M) surface is the structural explanation. **Closure mode C** (circular): the depth-2 gap is fully captured by an elementary fact already in the project's frame (bit_0 "free first gate" mechanism, S84 §"Mechanism: single-bit predictor advantage"); calibration formally verifies the explanation. Recommends footnote on `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`: 36th measure (depth-2 sign-threshold) DEVIATES from unbiased random but the deviation is fully captured by the trivial 1-bit oddness fact; pseudorandomness thesis stands "modulo the obvious mod-2 bias." **Net new content**: (a) verified S84 mechanism (bit_0 → depth-2 size) under direct calibrated control; (b) new mechanism prediction empirically confirmed (bit_0_acc-vs-min_M monotonic at fixed weight); (c) PRIMES-vs-calibrated indistinguishability removes the only known deviation in the 35+ measure battery from "structural" to "elementary parity" status. Spawned successor C7.a (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES) — N=8 calibrated extension. Cites E1.10, E3.13, E1.6, E1.4, S84. See experiments/circuit_complexity/sat_tc0_primes_n8_calibrated/. | 89 |
