    974	continuous-time quantum walk (CTQW; Childs 2009) generated by
    975	Hamiltonian `H = A_G` (adjacency) or `H = L_G` (Laplacian) has
    976	fundamentally different mixing phenomenology — Childs et al. 2003
    977	showed CTQW gives EXPONENTIAL speedup on glued binary trees where
    978	Szegedy gives only polynomial. Question: on the divisor graph `D_x`,
    979	coprime graph `C_x`, or Cayley graph of `(Z/NZ)*`, does the CTQW
    980	amplitude `|⟨prime | e^{-iHt} | seed⟩|^2` evolve to a primality-
    981	detecting concentration in time `O(polylog x)`?
    982	
    983	**Why frontier:** the §D.D4 closure exploited the Szegedy
    984	discriminant theorem `mixing ~ 1/√δ`. CTQW mixing instead depends
    985	on the SPECTRAL STRUCTURE (density of states, eigenvector overlap
