    756:| §D6 ATTACK_VECTORS — Gowers U^k uniformity norms of the bare prime indicator chi_P (cross-domain: additive combinatorics, Green-Tao-Ziegler U^{s+1} inverse theorem) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether chi_P deviates from random pseudorandomly under any Gowers norm at k <= 3 — the only family of "k-degree polynomial structure" tests untouched by the project's 35+ pseudorandomness measures. Computed normalized Gowers norms `Q^k(f) := ‖f‖_{U^k}^{2^k} / E[f]^{2^k}` on Z/NZ for chi_P, matched-density Bernoulli, Liouville indicator, and W-tricked chi_{W,1} (W ∈ {6, 30, 210}). U^2 via FFT identity `‖f‖_{U^2}^4 = (1/N^4) Σ_k |fhat(k)|^4` (O(N log N)) at N ∈ {2^10, 2^12, 2^14, 2^16, 2^18}; U^3 via recursion `‖f‖_{U^3}^8 = (1/N) Σ_h ‖Δ_h f‖_{U^2}^4` with `Δ_h f(x) = f(x)f(x+h)` (O(N^2 log N)) at N ∈ {2^10, 2^11, 2^12, 2^13}. **Hardy-Littlewood prediction**: `Q^k(chi_P) → S_k = Π_p α_p(k) / (1 - 1/p)^{2^k}` (singular series for {0,1}^k-cube prime k-tuple), where `α_p(k) = #{(x, h) ∈ (Z/p)^{k+1} : x + ε·h ≢ 0 mod p ∀ε ∈ {0,1}^k} / p^{k+1}`. Numerical truncated values: **S_2 = 2.300938** (P_max=100, 1e-5 truncation error), **S_3 = 54.116088** (P_max=47, 0.2% error). **Empirical Q^2(chi_P) trend**: 2.103 (N=2^10) → 2.132 (N=2^12) → 2.146 (N=2^14) → 2.149 (N=2^16) → 2.153 (N=2^18); monotonic increase toward S_2; gap S_2 - Q^2(chi_P) decays as O(1/log N) (from 0.198 at N=2^10 to 0.148 at N=2^18). **Q^2(Bernoulli) ~ 1 + O(1/N)** (1.049 → 1.008 across same range). **Q^3(chi_P) ≈ 35.5** stable across N ∈ [2^10, 2^13], well above Bernoulli's Q^3 → 1 but below S_3 = 54.12 due to slow finite-N convergence at U^3 (compounded log-factors). **Liouville**: Q^2(L) = 1.000 to 4 digits at N=2^10..2^12 — Gowers-uniform at U^2, consistent with Green-Tao Mobius/nilsequence orthogonality (the prime-parity indicator is structurally OPPOSITE to chi_P at U^k). **W-trick**: predicted `S^(W)_k = Π_{p∤W} α_p(k)/(1-1/p)^{2^k}`. At N=2^12, **W=210**: empirical Q^2(chi_{W,1}) = 1.0029 vs HL prediction 1.0023 (match within 0.1%); empirical Q^3 = 1.066 vs HL 1.029 (match within 4%, dominated by finite-N noise on Q^3). **W=30**: Q^2 = 1.005 vs 1.007, exact match. The W-trick empirically restores Gowers-uniformity to chi_P, exactly as the Green-Tao W-trick predicts for Lambda. **First instance in the project's pseudorandomness battery (after S84 circuit-depth gap at N=6) where chi_P deviates from random by a CLOSED-FORM, predicted, constant multiplicative factor**, with the deviation EXACTLY matching the Hardy-Littlewood box singular series. **Closure mode E**: U^k structure of chi_P provides only HL-level information, already conjecturally known; no additional bit of structure detected; algorithmic extraction of Q^k itself costs Θ(N^2 log N), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: Gowers norms (Gowers 2001) detect higher-order correlation structure invisible to the project's local statistics; the FFT identity for U^2 and recursion for U^3 are standard machinery from additive combinatorics. **Cited new EDGE: E2.13** (Q^k(chi_P) = S_k {0,1}^k-cube). Cites E1.10, E3.13, E7.1, E2.9, S84. Cross-domain refs: Gowers (2001); Green-Tao (arXiv:math/0606088); Green-Tao (arXiv:0807.1736); Green-Tao-Ziegler (arXiv:1009.3998); Hardy-Littlewood (1923). See experiments/information_theory/gowers_uk_chi_p_results.md. | 85 |
    761:| §D7 ATTACK_VECTORS — Determinantal point process (DPP) / permanantal counterpart fit to integer prime sequence (cross-domain: DPP theory, Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009, Soshnikov 2000, Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether chi_P admits a translation-invariant kernel representation R_2(t) = rho^2 ± K(t)^2 (DPP -, PPP +). Tested four progressively-flexible kernel hypotheses at N = 10^7. **F1 (DPP pair-level)**: K^2_DPP(t) = rho^2 - R_2(t) < 0 at ALL 15 admissible even t in [2, 30]; HL gives S(0, t) > 1 ⇒ R_2 > rho^2. Pair-level DPP infeasible. **F2 (PPP pair-level)**: K^2_PPP(t) = R_2(t) - rho^2 < 0 at ALL 14 odd t > 1 (R_2 ≈ 0). Pair-level PPP infeasible. Sign of (R_2 - rho^2) flips between odd/even — no real translation-invariant K. **F3 (PPP 3-point)** restricting to all-even sub-lattice where K^2_PPP > 0: permanent prediction R_3^PPP overshoots HL prediction R_3^HL = rho^3 S(0, t_1, t_2) by 7.5–79.2% across 19 admissible triples (max gap on 3-AP triples (0,6,12), (0,12,18), (0,18,24)). **F4 (real-signed K)**: with magnitudes |K(t)| = rho sqrt(S(0,t)-1) and signs s : t → ±1, required cross-term σ_req ∈ (-0.541, +0.769), NEVER ±1 (closest 0.769) at any of 19 admissible triples. Real signed K of right magnitudes fails universally. **F5 (complex Hermitian K)**: phases free; least-squares fit of φ over 13 distinct offsets (200 random starts, LM + trust-region) yields best max residual 0.0746 ≫ 0.01 noise floor. No globally consistent phase assignment. **Inadmissibility blindness**: PPP predicts non-zero R_3 for inadmissible triples like (0, 4, 14) (where ν_3 = 3 saturates) because pair correlations alone cannot detect multi-body admissibility. **Mechanism**: HL singular series factorises over PRIMES (∏_p α_p(0, t_1, ..., t_k) with α_p depending on ν_p = #distinct residues mod p); DPP/PPP correlations factorise over PAIRS. Pairwise admissibility ≠ triple admissibility. **Adds EDGE E2.16**: primes are NOT a translation-invariant DPP / PPP / signed-real-K / complex-Hermitian-K point process. FOURTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers, E2.14/S88 Anderson, E2.15/S92 algebraic immunity) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a FOURTH orthogonal mathematical category (point-process theory) AND at the 3-point level (prior three were 2-point). **Closure mode I**: HL prime-by-prime factorisation cannot reduce to pair-level kernel. Cross-domain ingredient (DPP) performed real work; first project use. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009 *Zeros of GAFs and DPPs* (AMS ULect 51); Soshnikov 2000 (arXiv:math/0002099); Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP. See experiments/constructions/primes_dpp_ppp_fit/primes_dpp_ppp_fit_results.md. | 95 |
    763:| §D2 ATTACK_VECTORS — Persistent homology of Takens-embedded normalised prime gap sequence (cross-domain: persistent homology / Vietoris-Rips filtration, Carlsson 2009 BAMS, Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010, Bauer 2021 ripser arXiv:1908.02518) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether the prime gap sequence carries persistent topological features distinguishable from a matched-density Poisson process. Protocol: M=2000 consecutive normalised gaps x_n = (p_{n+1}-p_n)/log(p_n) starting near p ≈ 10^6 (sieve to N_max=10^7); Takens-embed at delay 1 in d ∈ {2, 3, 4}; ripser persistent H_0 / H_1 with thresh ∈ {4.0, 5.0}; baselines K=20 each: B1 IID Exp(1), B2 random permutation of empirical window (preserves marginal, kills serial correlation). Pre-registered F3 (PRIMES > 3σ from BOTH B1 AND B2 on at least one summary) HOLDS: at d=3, M=2000, x≈10^6: T0 (total H_0 persistence) z(B1) = -10.31, z(B2) = -8.70 (rank 0/20 in both); T1 (total H_1 persistence) z(B1) = -4.20, z(B2) = -11.99 (rank 0/20). Effect robust at second window x ≈ 5·10^6 (T0 z(B2) = -7.58, T1 z(B2) = -8.69) and across d ∈ {2, 3, 4} (T0 z(B2) ∈ [-8.7, -5.1]). Scaling sweep M ∈ {500, 1000, 2000, 4000} shows z-scores grow super-linearly (M=4000 gives T0 z(B1) = -17.8) — signal at least linear in window size. **Mechanism:** primes are MORE clustered (smaller T0) and have FEWER persistent loops (smaller T1) than Poisson-gap and gap-permuted controls. The B2 control isolates serial correlation; T0/T1 deficit relative to B2 is the HL k-tuple admissibility component (consecutive gaps repeat residue patterns more often than random, creating geometric self-similarity in delay-embedding cloud). **Adds EDGE E2.17**: PH of prime gap delay embedding deviates ≥ 5σ from IID Exp(1) AND from gap-marginal-permuted control across multiple windows, dimensions, and sample sizes. FIFTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13 Gowers, E2.14 Anderson, E2.15 algebraic immunity, E2.16 DPP failure) of HL equidistribution structure in chi_P, now in a FIFTH orthogonal mathematical category (algebraic-topological / metric-space geometry). **Closure mode I**: PH is a measurement instrument, not an algorithm — no closed-form polylog evaluator suggested; VR-PH costs O(M^3) worst-case. Cross-domain ingredient (PH on Takens embedding via ripser) performed real work; first project quantitative measurement (S10 mention was qualitative, gtda-based, no baseline). Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E2.16, E7.7. Cross-domain refs: Carlsson 2009 BAMS 46(2); Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010 *Computational Topology*; Bauer 2021 J. Appl. Comput. Topol. 5 (arXiv:1908.02518); Cohen-Steiner-Edelsbrunner-Harer 2007 (PH stability). See experiments/topological/persistent_homology_chi_p/persistent_homology_chi_p_results.md. | 96 |
