    763:| §D2 ATTACK_VECTORS — Persistent homology of Takens-embedded normalised prime gap sequence (cross-domain: persistent homology / Vietoris-Rips filtration, Carlsson 2009 BAMS, Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010, Bauer 2021 ripser arXiv:1908.02518) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether the prime gap sequence carries persistent topological features distinguishable from a matched-density Poisson process. Protocol: M=2000 consecutive normalised gaps x_n = (p_{n+1}-p_n)/log(p_n) starting near p ≈ 10^6 (sieve to N_max=10^7); Takens-embed at delay 1 in d ∈ {2, 3, 4}; ripser persistent H_0 / H_1 with thresh ∈ {4.0, 5.0}; baselines K=20 each: B1 IID Exp(1), B2 random permutation of empirical window (preserves marginal, kills serial correlation). Pre-registered F3 (PRIMES > 3σ from BOTH B1 AND B2 on at least one summary) HOLDS: at d=3, M=2000, x≈10^6: T0 (total H_0 persistence) z(B1) = -10.31, z(B2) = -8.70 (rank 0/20 in both); T1 (total H_1 persistence) z(B1) = -4.20, z(B2) = -11.99 (rank 0/20). Effect robust at second window x ≈ 5·10^6 (T0 z(B2) = -7.58, T1 z(B2) = -8.69) and across d ∈ {2, 3, 4} (T0 z(B2) ∈ [-8.7, -5.1]). Scaling sweep M ∈ {500, 1000, 2000, 4000} shows z-scores grow super-linearly (M=4000 gives T0 z(B1) = -17.8) — signal at least linear in window size. **Mechanism:** primes are MORE clustered (smaller T0) and have FEWER persistent loops (smaller T1) than Poisson-gap and gap-permuted controls. The B2 control isolates serial correlation; T0/T1 deficit relative to B2 is the HL k-tuple admissibility component (consecutive gaps repeat residue patterns more often than random, creating geometric self-similarity in delay-embedding cloud). **Adds EDGE E2.17**: PH of prime gap delay embedding deviates ≥ 5σ from IID Exp(1) AND from gap-marginal-permuted control across multiple windows, dimensions, and sample sizes. FIFTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13 Gowers, E2.14 Anderson, E2.15 algebraic immunity, E2.16 DPP failure) of HL equidistribution structure in chi_P, now in a FIFTH orthogonal mathematical category (algebraic-topological / metric-space geometry). **Closure mode I**: PH is a measurement instrument, not an algorithm — no closed-form polylog evaluator suggested; VR-PH costs O(M^3) worst-case. Cross-domain ingredient (PH on Takens embedding via ripser) performed real work; first project quantitative measurement (S10 mention was qualitative, gtda-based, no baseline). Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E2.16, E7.7. Cross-domain refs: Carlsson 2009 BAMS 46(2); Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010 *Computational Topology*; Bauer 2021 J. Appl. Comput. Topol. 5 (arXiv:1908.02518); Cohen-Steiner-Edelsbrunner-Harer 2007 (PH stability). See experiments/topological/persistent_homology_chi_p/persistent_homology_chi_p_results.md. | 96 |
