    764	| §G1 ATTACK_VECTORS — Liouville Anderson Lyapunov: spectral signature of Möbius pseudorandomness (cross-domain: Anderson localisation [reused S88] + Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality, Green-Tao 2012 *Annals* 175 = arXiv:0807.1736; Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures; Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla = arXiv:1509.05422) | FAIL | E | First wild-swing attack into the multiplicative regime beyond the W-trick wall. Setup identical to S88/E2.14 except potential is the **centered multiplicative encoding** V(n) = lambda(n) ∈ {-1, +1} (mean → 0 by PNT for Liouville, variance = 1 exactly, NOT the {0, 1} encoding S88 used). Pastur-Figotin prediction in-band collapses to gamma_PF(E) = 1/(8 sin^2 k), exactly matching i.i.d. Rademacher ±1 baseline. Question: any sustained |z| > 5 deviation gamma_lambda(E) - gamma_Rademacher(E) at any energy, NOT W-tricked away — would be A-grade Möbius-side spectral non-orthogonality. **Empirical at 51 energies in E ∈ [-2.95, 2.95], three sample sizes: max |z| = 1.78 (N=10^5, 50 seeds, argmax E=-0.236), 2.16 (N=3·10^5, 50 seeds, argmax +0.118), 2.04 (N=10^6, 100 seeds, argmax -2.006).** All below 51-energy Bonferroni threshold z = 3.16. Argmax energy WANDERS between runs (statistical, not arithmetic). chi^2 / K = 0.49-0.69 (Rademacher prediction = 1; lambda is sub-Rademacher). L^2 distance from Rademacher mean: lambda lies at empirical p ≈ {0.58, 0.86, 0.59} of the seed-to-seed Rademacher distribution. Pastur-Figotin agreement: gamma_lambda / gamma_PF = 0.9317 (std 0.32) inside band, identical to gamma_Rademacher_mean / gamma_PF = 0.9309 to 4 decimals. **Independent off-spectral check (two-point Chowla aggregate at N=10^6, h=1..16): Σ z_h^2 = 4.77 vs Rademacher chi^2_16 mean 16, std sqrt(32) ≈ 5.7** — empirical p ≈ 0.997, lambda is *more Rademacher-like than Rademacher* on Chowla. All 16 individual lag z's |z_h| ≤ 1.11. **Stark contrast with E2.14 (chi_P, S88) at same N=10^5 grid: chi_P max |z| = 88.5σ at locked E=0.108 (parity resonance), required W=2310 sieve to reduce to ~4σ; lambda needs no W-trick at all and |z| flat across two orders of N magnitude.** **Mechanism (structural reason for closure mode E):** Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality (Green-Tao 2012, arXiv:0807.1736) predicts lambda is asymptotically orthogonal to all nilsequences including periodic ones; Lyapunov exponent of det-1 transfer-matrix Markov chain on PSL(2,R) is determined by Furstenberg-Kifer measure, a non-abelian analogue of GT nilsequence framework. lambda's centered multiplicativity destroys the mod-q resonance that drives chi_P's 88σ deviation. Sub-Rademacher Chowla aggregate (Σ z² = 4.77 ≪ 16) is consistent with Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla theorem (arXiv:1509.05422). **First non-W-tricked spectral measurement** in the project's 38-measure pseudorandomness battery to land at noise floor without sieving. **Pairs with E2.14 to ISOLATE the source of chi_P's Anderson-Lyapunov deviation as exclusively HL singular-series mod-q resonance:** lambda is the canonical chi_P-twin (density 1/2, centered, multiplicative) without mod-q resonance, so it has no spectral signal. **Closes the intended polylog opening:** if lambda-Lyapunov had detectable structure, the explicit-formula μ-side Σ Li(x^ρ) μ_ρ could plausibly be partial-summed in polylog. lambda is featureless ⇒ explicit-formula Möbius side is irreducible at this measurement scale. **Adds EDGE E2.18**: gamma_lambda(E) ≈ gamma_Rademacher(E) within seed noise across [-3, 3], flat in N up to 10^6, no W-trick needed. **Cross-domain ingredient (Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality) performed real work**: first project use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded UNUSED → USED E. Cites E2.14, E2.13, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators* AMS GSM 168; Furstenberg-Kifer 1983; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:0807.1736 (Möbius nilsequence orthogonality, primary); Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures (Möbius randomness conjecture); Tao 2016 Forum Math Pi 4 e8 = arXiv:1509.05422 (logarithmic-Chowla); Tao-Teräväinen 2017 arXiv:1708.02610. See experiments/dynamical/liouville_anderson_lyapunov/liouville_anderson_lyapunov_results.md. | 100 |
