    7	
    8	## The objects
    9	
    10	### Brandt's hypothesis class (the function class for which the lower bound applies)
    11	
    12	The Brandt 2024 lower bound is **specifically** the language
    13	
    14	```
    15	    MKtP_U  :=  { (y, k) in {0,1}^m x [m]  :  Kt_U(y) <= k }
    16	```
    17	
    18	where `U` is a fixed prefix-free universal Turing machine (UTM) and
    19	
    20	```
    21	    Kt_U(x)  :=  min { |Pi| + ceil(log2 t)  :  U(Pi) outputs x in <= t steps }.
    22	```
    23	
    24	Brandt's main theorem (Theorem 1) is
    25	
    26	> `MKtP_U  not in  DTIME[O(n)]`     (unconditional)
    27	
    28	with corollaries:
    29	- `MKtP_U  not in  DTIME[O(n^2)]` if the underlying machine model has a
    30	  linear-time universal simulation (e.g. RAMs).
