 operator with V=chi_P deviates from random Lyapunov by a quantity that W-tricks down to noise. **Closure mode E**: deviation IS the spectral signature of Hardy-Littlewood / Bombieri-Vinogradov equidistribution mod q; no additional spectral structure beyond what equidistribution already gives; algorithmic gamma extraction costs Theta(N), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: transfer-matrix product / Lyapunov machinery (Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators*, Furstenberg-Kifer 1983) had never been applied to chi_P; the spectral signature of the W-trick at the Anderson-Lyapunov level is novel. **PROVIDES SECOND INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION** (after E2.13/S85) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, in a category orthogonal to additive combinatorics. Cites E2.13, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 (AMS GSM 168); Furstenberg-Kifer 1983 Israel J. Math. 46; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/dynamical/anderson_localisation_chi_p/anderson_localisation_chi_p_results.md. | 88 |
    | §B1 ATTACK_VECTORS — slice rank / Croot-Lev-Pach polynomial method on chi_P, via algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (cross-domain: cap-set polynomial method, Tao slice rank, Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether the cap-set polynomial-method machinery yields a polylog primality witness via low-degree annihilators of chi_P. Three structurally distinct invariants: (1) algebraic immunity AI(chi_P) over F_2 (smallest deg g with g·chi_P==0 or g·(1+chi_P)==0); (2) F_p multilinear ANF degree on (F_p)^k via base-p expansion; (3) slice rank brackets via Tao 2016 flattening lower bound + greedy upper bound. **Main empirical finding**: AI(chi_P, N) = 2 for ALL N in [4, 13] while AI(matched-density Bernoulli) grows as Theta(log_2(1/rho)) — reaching 4 at N=11/12 with zero std. Liouville+ AI grows like random; Mobius!=0 also has constant AI=2. **Mechanism (extracted via nullspace recovery)**: the unique smallest annihilator is the SAME polynomial g(x) = (1 + x_0)(1 + x_1) for every N >= 5, which equals 1 iff n ≡ 0 mod 4. The annihilation works because no prime > 2 is divisible by 4 (and chi_P(2) gets killed by bit_1=1). AI(chi_P)=2 is *exactly* the polynomial-method encoding of the trivial mod-4 sieve fact; same g annihilates Mobius!=0 because squarefree numbers exclude multiples of 4. Liouville+ does NOT inherit this since lambda(4)=+1. **W-trick correction CONFIRMS deviation is mod-q structure**: at W=6, b∈{1,5} and W=30, b∈{1,7,11}, AI(chi_P_{W,b}) tracks AI(random) within ±1 across N=8..11; many cells exact match with zero std (e.g. W=6 b=1 N=11: chi_P=5, random=5.00 std 0). **F_p multilinear ANF degree**: chi_P near-saturates max possible degree (p-1)·k at all tested (p,k) other than (3,3) where deg drops 1 below random max, and (5,3) similar single-degree drop. **Slice rank brackets**: at p=2 non-informative (2-row flattenings cap rank at 2 trivially, both chi_P and random); at p=3 chi_P matches random for k>=3. **Same structural reason as E2.13 (Gowers, S85), E2.14 (Anderson, S88)**: chi_P deviation is fully captured by small-modulus residue-class structure; the polynomial-method invariant gives no additional bit beyond mod-q. **Adds EDGE E2.15**: AI_F_2(chi_P) = 2 for all N >= 4 with explicit annihilator (1+x_0)(1+x_1); W-trick at W>=6 removes deviation. THIRD INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers and E2.14/S88 Anderson) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a third orthogonal mathematical category (Boolean polynomial method / algebraic cryptanalysis). **Closure mode E**: AI deviation IS the polynomial-method encoding of the mod-4 sieve fact; no additional polynomial-method content beyond mod-q. AI extraction itself is exponential time in N (LP over 2^N x sum_i C(N,i) F_2 monomial-evaluation matrix), not polylog. **Cross-domain ingredient performed real work**: Croot-Lev-Pach / Tao slice rank / Courtois-Meier algebraic immunity machinery had never been applied to chi_P; the polynomial-method signature of the W-trick at AI level is novel. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Croot-Lev-Pach arXiv:1605.01506; Tao 2016 blog (slice rank); Ellenberg-Gijswijt 2017 Annals 185, 339; Courtois-Meier 2003 Eurocrypt LNCS 2656; Green-Tao arXiv:math/0606088 (W-trick). See experiments/algebraic/algebraic_immunity_chi_p/algebraic_immunity_chi_p_results.md. | 92 |
    | §D7 ATTACK_VECTORS — Determinantal point process (DPP) / permanantal counterpart fit to integer prime sequence (cross-domain: DPP theory, Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009, Soshnikov 2000, Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether chi_P admits a translation-invariant kernel representation R_2(t) = rho^2 ± K(t)^2 (DPP -, PPP +). Tested four progressively-flexible kernel hypotheses at N = 10^7. **F1 (DPP pair-level)**: K^2_DPP(t) = rho^2 - R_2(t) < 0 at ALL 15 admissible even t in [2, 30]; HL gives S(0, t) > 1 ⇒ R_2 > rho^2. Pair-level DPP infeasible. **F2 (PPP pair-level)**: K^2_PPP(t) = R_2(t) - rho^2 < 0 at ALL 14 odd t > 1 (R_2 ≈ 0). Pair-level PPP infeasible. Sign of (R_2 - rho^2) flips between odd/even — no real translation-invariant K. **F3 (PPP 3-point)** restricting to all-even sub-lattice where K^2_PPP > 0: permanent prediction R_3^PPP overshoots HL prediction R_3^HL = rho^3 S(0, t_1, t_2) by 7.5–79.2% across 19 admissible triples (max gap on 3-AP triples (0,6,12), (0,12,18), (0,18,24)). **F4 (real-signed K)**: with magnitudes |K(t)| = rho sqrt(S(0,t)-1) and signs s : t → ±1, required cross-term σ_req ∈ (-0.541, +0.769), NEVER ±1 (closest 0.769) at any of 19 admissible triples. Real signed K of right magnitudes fails universally. **F5 (complex Hermitian K)**: phases free; least-squares fit of φ over 13 distinct offsets (200 random starts, LM + trust-region) yields best max residual 0.0746 ≫ 0.01 noise floor. No globally consistent phase assignment. **Inadmissibility blindness**: PPP predicts non-zero R_3 for inadmissible triples like (0, 4, 14) (where ν_3 = 3 saturates) because pair correlations alone cannot detect multi-body admissibility. **Mechanism**: HL singular series factorises over PRIMES (∏_p α_p(0, t_1, ..., t_k) with α_p depending on ν_p = #distinct residues mod p); DPP/PPP correlations factorise over PAIRS. Pairwise admissibility ≠ triple admissibility. **Adds EDGE E2.16**: primes are NOT a translation-invariant DPP / PPP / signed-real-K / complex-Hermitian-K point process. FOURTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13/S85 Gowers, E2.14/S88 Anderson, E2.15/S92 algebraic immunity) that chi_P structure = HL equidistribution mod q, now in a FOURTH orthogonal mathematical category (point-process theory) AND at the 3-point level (prior three were 2-point). **Closure mode I**: HL prime-by-prime factorisation cannot reduce to pair-level kernel. Cross-domain ingredient (DPP) performed real work; first project use. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E1.10, E3.13, E7.1. Cross-domain refs: Hough-Krishnapur-Peres-Virag 2009 *Zeros of GAFs and DPPs* (AMS ULect 51); Soshnikov 2000 (arXiv:math/0002099); Vere-Jones 1997 alpha-DPP. See experiments/constructions/primes_dpp_ppp_fit/primes_dpp_ppp_fit_results.md. | 95 |
    
    | §D2 ATTACK_VECTORS — Persistent homology of Takens-embedded normalised prime gap sequence (cross-domain: persistent homology / Vietoris-Rips filtration, Carlsson 2009 BAMS, Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010, Bauer 2021 ripser arXiv:1908.02518) | FAIL | I | Frontier attack on whether the prime gap sequence carries persistent topological features distinguishable from a matched-density Poisson process. Protocol: M=2000 consecutive normalised gaps x_n = (p_{n+1}-p_n)/log(p_n) starting near p ≈ 10^6 (sieve to N_max=10^7); Takens-embed at delay 1 in d ∈ {2, 3, 4}; ripser persistent H_0 / H_1 with thresh ∈ {4.0, 5.0}; baselines K=20 each: B1 IID Exp(1), B2 random permutation of empirical window (preserves marginal, kills serial correlation). Pre-registered F3 (PRIMES > 3σ from BOTH B1 AND B2 on at least one summary) HOLDS: at d=3, M=2000, x≈10^6: T0 (total H_0 persistence) z(B1) = -10.31, z(B2) = -8.70 (rank 0/20 in both); T1 (total H_1 persistence) z(B1) = -4.20, z(B2) = -11.99 (rank 0/20). Effect robust at second window x ≈ 5·10^6 (T0 z(B2) = -7.58, T1 z(B2) = -8.69) and across d ∈ {2, 3, 4} (T0 z(B2) ∈ [-8.7, -5.1]). Scaling sweep M ∈ {500, 1000, 2000, 4000} shows z-scores grow super-linearly (M=4000 gives T0 z(B1) = -17.8) — signal at least linear in window size. **Mechanism:** primes are MORE clustered (smaller T0) and have FEWER persistent loops (smaller T1) than Poisson-gap and gap-permuted controls. The B2 control isolates serial correlation; T0/T1 deficit relative to B2 is the HL k-tuple admissibility component (consecutive gaps repeat residue patterns more often than random, creating geometric self-similarity in delay-embedding cloud). **Adds EDGE E2.17**: PH of prime gap delay embedding deviates ≥ 5σ from IID Exp(1) AND from gap-marginal-permuted control across multiple windows, dimensions, and sample sizes. FIFTH INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION (after E2.13 Gowers, E2.14 Anderson, E2.15 algebraic immunity, E2.16 DPP failure) of HL equidistribution structure in chi_P, now in a FIFTH orthogonal mathematical category (algebraic-topological / metric-space geometry). **Closure mode I**: PH is a measurement instrument, not an algorithm — no closed-form polylog evaluator suggested; VR-PH costs O(M^3) worst-case. Cross-domain ingredient (PH on Takens embedding via ripser) performed real work; first project quantitative measurement (S10 mention was qualitative, gtda-based, no baseline). Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E2.16, E7.7. Cross-domain refs: Carlsson 2009 BAMS 46(2); Edelsbrunner-Harer 2010 *Computational Topology*; Bauer 2021 J. Appl. Comput. Topol. 5 (arXiv:1908.02518); Cohen-Steiner-Edelsbrunner-Harer 2007 (PH stability). See experiments/topological/persistent_homology_chi_p/persistent_homology_chi_p_results.md. | 96 |
    | §D13 ATTACK_VECTORS — Subword (factor) complexity p_w(n) of chi_P as a binary infinite word, with topological entropy h_w (cross-domain: symbolic dynamics on prime sequences, Lind-Marcus 1995 *Symbolic Dynamics and Coding* CUP, Cassaigne-Nicolas 2010 "Factor complexity" CANT vol. 135, Morse-Hedlund 1938 *Amer. J. Math.* 60) | FAIL | E | Frontier attack on whether the prime indicator binary word w = chi_P(2)chi_P(3)... has subword complexity p_w(n) := #{distinct length-n factors of w} that deviates from matched-density Bernoulli — the canonical combinatorial-on-words test (no published value for chi_P; Wikipedia "Complexity function"). Promotes the informal CLOSED_PATHS line 181 "Symbolic dynamics — near-random block complexity (S4)" to a precise quantitative measurement with finite-N value, K=20 baselines, and full W-trick cascade. Protocol: sieve to N = 5·10^6 (348,513 primes); five chi_P-derived streams — RAW (chi_P(2..N), L=4,999,999, density 0.0697); ODD (chi_P(2k+1), L=2,499,999, density 0.139); W6 (chi_P(6n+1), L=833,334, density 0.209); W30 (chi_P(30n+1), L=166,667, density 0.261); W210 (chi_P(210n+1), L=23,810, density 0.305). Per stream, n ∈ [1, 22] vectorised rolling-encoding factor count (numpy uint64; cost O(nL), memory O(L)); K=20 random permutations of the stream (B2: preserves density and 1-marginal exactly, kills all >1-gram structure) and K=20 iid Bernoulli matched-density samples (B1). Pre-registered F3 (PRIMES > 3σ from BOTH B1 AND B2 at every n in [n_lo, n_hi] with n_hi ≥ 18, on at least one of {ODD, W6, W30}) HOLDS at z >> 3σ for ODD (max |z_perm| = 277 at n=7), W6 (|z_perm| = 121 at n=8), and W30 (|z_perm| = 25 at n=17). Cascade |z_perm| at peak across streams: RAW 132.7 → ODD 277.1 → W6 120.5 → W30 24.8 → W210 8.4 — clean monotone reduction by ~1.5 orders of magnitude across W ∈ {1, 6, 30, 210}. Ratio p_chi(22) / p_perm_mean(22): RAW 0.018 (98% deficit, parity-driven), ODD 0.216 (78% deficit, mod-3 in odd-stream), W6 0.806 (19% deficit), W30 0.994, W210 1.011 (≈ noise; sign flips above n=17 indicating saturation). Effective topological entropy h_eff(n) := log_2 p_w(n) / n at W=210, n=22: chi 0.6581 vs perm 0.6574 (match to 0.001, i.e. log_2(L)/22 saturation). **Mechanism**: subword complexity counts distinct configurations of primes inside a sliding length-n window; chi_P configurations are constrained by mod-p admissibility for p ≤ n (only one prime can be a multiple of p, except p itself). The W = primorial(p_k) sieve removes those constraints for p ≤ p_k, monotonically erasing the deficit. Same Hardy-Littlewood k-tuple admissibility engine that drives E2.13 Gowers, E2.14 Anderson, E2.16 DPP failure, E2.17 PH. Residual |z_perm| = 8.4 at W=210, n=12 is consistent with `O(1/log N)` HL singular-series tail. **Adds EDGE E2.19**: subword complexity of chi_P deviates ≥ 100σ from Bernoulli matched-density on raw/W6 streams; W=210 W-trick reduces to ≤ 8.4σ at finite L = 2.4·10^4. **38th pseudorandomness measure**, **SIXTH orthogonal HL-detection family** (after E2.13 Gowers, E2.14 Anderson, E2.15 algebraic immunity, E2.16 DPP, E2.17 PH), in a NEW mathematical category (symbolic-dynamics / factor-complexity / topological-entropy). **Closure mode E**: subword complexity at given window length is O(L log L) — no polylog opening; W-trick fingerprint encodes only HL information already known. **Cross-domain ingredient (factor complexity / topological entropy of binary words) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §5 upgraded PROPOSED → USED E with edge E2.19. Cites E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E2.16, E2.17, E2.18, E7.7. Cross-domain refs: Cassaigne-Nicolas 2010 "Factor complexity" CANT vol. 135 (Cambridge); Lind-Marcus 1995 *An Introduction to Symbolic Dynamics and Coding* (Cambridge); Morse-Hedlund 1938-40 "Symbolic Dynamics" *Amer. J. Math.* 60. See experiments/dynamical/subword_complexity_chi_p/subword_complexity_chi_p_results.md. | 104 |
    | §G1 ATTACK_VECTORS — Liouville Anderson Lyapunov: spectral signature of Möbius pseudorandomness (cross-domain: Anderson localisation [reused S88] + Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality, Green-Tao 2012 *Annals* 175 = arXiv:0807.1736; Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures; Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla = arXiv:1509.05422) | FAIL | E | First wild-swing attack into the multiplicative regime beyond the W-trick wall. Setup identical to S88/E2.14 except potential is the **centered multiplicative encoding** V(n) = lambda(n) ∈ {-1, +1} (mean → 0 by PNT for Liouville, variance = 1 exactly, NOT the {0, 1} encoding S88 used). Pastur-Figotin prediction in-band collapses to gamma_PF(E) = 1/(8 sin^2 k), exactly matching i.i.d. Rademacher ±1 baseline. Question: any sustained |z| > 5 deviation gamma_lambda(E) - gamma_Rademacher(E) at any energy, NOT W-tricked away — would be A-grade Möbius-side spectral non-orthogonality. **Empirical at 51 energies in E ∈ [-2.95, 2.95], three sample sizes: max |z| = 1.78 (N=10^5, 50 seeds, argmax E=-0.236), 2.16 (N=3·10^5, 50 seeds, argmax +0.118), 2.04 (N=10^6, 100 seeds, argmax -2.006).** All below 51-energy Bonferroni threshold z = 3.16. Argmax energy WANDERS between runs (statistical, not arithmetic). chi^2 / K = 0.49-0.69 (Rademacher prediction = 1; lambda is sub-Rademacher). L^2 distance from Rademacher mean: lambda lies at empirical p ≈ {0.58, 0.86, 0.59} of the seed-to-seed Rademacher distribution. Pastur-Figotin agreement: gamma_lambda / gamma_PF = 0.9317 (std 0.32) inside band, identical to gamma_Rademacher_mean / gamma_PF = 0.9309 to 4 decimals. **Independent off-spectral check (two-point Chowla aggregate at N=10^6, h=1..16): Σ z_h^2 = 4.77 vs Rademacher chi^2_16 mean 16, std sqrt(32) ≈ 5.7** — empirical p ≈ 0.997, lambda is *more Rademacher-like than Rademacher* on Chowla. All 16 individual lag z's |z_h| ≤ 1.11. **Stark contrast with E2.14 (chi_P, S88) at same N=10^5 grid: chi_P max |z| = 88.5σ at locked E=0.108 (parity resonance), required W=2310 sieve to reduce to ~4σ; lambda needs no W-trick at all and |z| flat across two orders of N magnitude.** **Mechanism (structural reason for closure mode E):** Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality (Green-Tao 2012, arXiv:0807.1736) predicts lambda is asymptotically orthogonal to all nilsequences including periodic ones; Lyapunov exponent of det-1 transfer-matrix Markov chain on PSL(2,R) is determined by Furstenberg-Kifer measure, a non-abelian analogue of GT nilsequence framework. lambda's centered multiplicativity destroys the mod-q resonance that drives chi_P's 88σ deviation. Sub-Rademacher Chowla aggregate (Σ z² = 4.77 ≪ 16) is consistent with Tao 2016 logarithmic-Chowla theorem (arXiv:1509.05422). **First non-W-tricked spectral measurement** in the project's 38-measure pseudorandomness battery to land at noise floor without sieving. **Pairs with E2.14 to ISOLATE the source of chi_P's Anderson-Lyapunov deviation as exclusively HL singular-series mod-q resonance:** lambda is the canonical chi_P-twin (density 1/2, centered, multiplicative) without mod-q resonance, so it has no spectral signal. **Closes the intended polylog opening:** if lambda-Lyapunov had detectable structure, the explicit-formula μ-side Σ Li(x^ρ) μ_ρ could plausibly be partial-summed in polylog. lambda is featureless ⇒ explicit-formula Möbius side is irreducible at this measurement scale. **Adds EDGE E2.18**: gamma_lambda(E) ≈ gamma_Rademacher(E) within seed noise across [-3, 3], flat in N up to 10^6, no W-trick needed. **Cross-domain ingredient (Möbius/nilsequence orthogonality) performed real work**: first project use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded UNUSED → USED E. Cites E2.14, E2.13, E1.10, E3.13. Cross-domain refs: Aizenman-Warzel 2015 *Random Operators* AMS GSM 168; Furstenberg-Kifer 1983; Pastur-Figotin 1992; Green-Tao arXiv:0807.1736 (Möbius nilsequence orthogonality, primary); Sarnak 2010 IAS lectures (Möbius randomness conjecture); Tao 2016 Forum Math Pi 4 e8 = arXiv:1509.05422 (logarithmic-Chowla); Tao-Teräväinen 2017 arXiv:1708.02610. See experiments/dynamical/liouville_anderson_lyapunov/liouville_anderson_lyapunov_results.md. | 100 |
