sure mode E**: Maynard's main theorem is `Σ w·χ_P ≥ c·Σ w` (averaged); pointwise content of w(n) is bounded by aggregate-vs-pointwise loss factor that depends on the F-eigenvalue ratio, not on F-shape. Empirical AUC_oddN ≤ 0.69 across all θ confirms this loss is irreducible; maynard_sym attempt did not improve over selberg_gpy. **Refines E6.7 (sieve pebbling)** by closing the most refined Selberg-sieve descendant; **reduces to E5.3 (MPOW)** via divisor-enumeration cost; **closes the project's only open problem (PRIMES in TC⁰) along the sieve-route attack family**, completing the four-family closure {AKS-modulus E7.10, Brandt MKtP E5.8, convergence-acceleration E7.11, **Maynard sieve E7.14**}. **Cross-domain ingredient (multidim GPY-Maynard sieve) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; status in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md upgraded PROPOSED → USED E with edge E7.14. **Adds EDGE E7.14**: Maynard 2015 multidim weight is aggregate-not-pointwise (AUC_oddN ∈ [0.66, 0.69]) AND requires Ω(N^{θ-o(1)}) divisor-enumeration cost per single n (sub-poly, not polylog) for any θ > 0 with non-trivial weight. Cites E6.7, E5.3, E7.10. Cross-domain refs: Maynard 2015 *Annals* 181:383 = arXiv:1311.4600; Polymath8b 2014 arXiv:1407.4897; Pascadi 2025 (E3.12). See experiments/sieve/maynard_weight_pointwise/maynard_weight_pointwise_results.md. | 116 |
